`1result.sql` is the best choice because  

• it explicitly filters on `tr.direction = 'I'`, guaranteeing that only one travel direction is used, which the task requires;  
• it correctly restricts trips to those where the Clay stop’s sequence precedes the Sacramento stop’s sequence;  
• it then returns the earliest departure from Clay and latest arrival at Sacramento, grouped by trip headsign (the requested field) and formatted as HH:MM:SS.  

The other two queries do not enforce the single‑direction rule (0result.sql and 2result.sql), so 1result.sql is the only query that fully satisfies all conditions.

```plaintext
1result.sql
